program leak_frame_temps

? Frame-temporary discipline (unified memory plan, leak suite): string
? concat, split results and array literals created inside a loop must be
? freed per iteration — block-exit cleanup plus split-piece ownership.
? Under valgrind this program must report zero lost bytes; see
? tools/mem_check.sh and MEMORY_BASELINE.md. Functional output pins the
? computation so the loop cannot be optimized away.

@ frame_work |n:int| int:
	total: 0
	loop i:0 to n do
		s: "entity-" + "x"
		parts: s.split|"-"|
		arr: [i, i + 1, i + 2]
		arr.push|i|
		total = total + arr.length + parts.length
	$
	return total
$

@ main ||:
	expected: []
	r: frame_work|200|
	print|r|
	expected.push|"1200"|
	print|expected|
$
